From 87b1766d1cbdced1c612813c936f3c5f00a6c4a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 06:49:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/15] perf(pfm): skip rendering work of empty plates, trash
 cans and microwaves

renderStatic draws nothing for empty stacks, so these renderers return
before their balanced pose push/pop, light, registry and recipe work when
their contents are empty, leaving PFM's public itemStack field as PFM
would. A filled trash can reads the light at its fixed position once per
frame instead of nine times, and a running microwave reuses its first
recipe lookup for the other two in the same condition. The new config is
client-only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
